Let $BC=x$. By the angle bisector theorem $\dfrac{AF}{FB}=\dfrac{CA}{CB}=\dfrac{6}{x}$, and $\dfrac{BD}{DC}=1$. By Ceva's theorem for the concurrent cevians $AD$, $BE$, $CF$,
\[
\dfrac{AF}{FB}\cdot\dfrac{BD}{DC}\cdot\dfrac{CE}{EA}=1\ \Longrightarrow\ \dfrac{CE}{EA}=\dfrac {x}{6}\ \Longrightarrow\ AE=\dfrac{6\cdot6}{6+x}=\dfrac{36}{x+6}.
\]

